  "description": "File upload storage for ASP.NET Core and .NET: keep user uploads on disk, in S3-compatible storage or in Azure Blob Storage, with a row per file in your database. Save an upload in one call and get back a StoredFile row on the application's own database; hand out a public URL, a temporary URL that expires, or a download behind your own authorization check. Files go to a directory on the deploy volume by default, or to S3-compatible storage (AWS, Cloudflare R2, Backblaze B2, MinIO) or Azure Blob Storage by configuration — with no cloud SDK behind it. Content types are sniffed from the bytes rather than trusted from the browser, and only images, audio and video are ever served inline. Server-side; pairs with EF Core and SQLite.",
